# OKR-Driven Executive System

**Enterprise-Grade Autonomous OKR Execution Platform**

- **Status**: Phase 0 (Strategic Planning Complete) ✅
- **Architecture**: Hexagonal + SOLID + Event-Driven
- **Ready for**: Phase 1 (Abstractions Implementation)
- **Language**: Python 3.11+
- **License**: MIT

---

## Quick Start (Developers)

```bash
# 1. Clone and navigate
cd ~/hermes-agent/projects/okr-executive-system

# 2. Setup development environment
make setup-dev

# 3. Run tests
make test

# 4. Run linters
make lint
```

---

## What This System Does

```
OKR Input (JSON)
  ↓
Parse & Validate (OKREngine)
  ↓
Research Solutions (ResearchEngine) [Expert Agents]
  ↓
Create Hierarchical Plan (PlanningEngine) [Pluggable Mental Models]
  ↓
Allocate Tasks Optimally (ExecutionEngine) [VCG Algorithm]
  ↓
Execute with Full Cognitive System (Accountable Agents)
  ↓
Generate & Submit PR (ReviewEngine)
  ↓
Calculate KPIs (MetricsEngine)
  ↓
Output: PR + Complete Audit Trail + KPIs
```

---

## Architecture

**See**: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`

### Key Decisions (ADRs)

- **ADR-O-001**: DuckDB for data store (columnar, analytics)
- **ADR-O-002**: NATS JetStream for events (persistence, replay)
- **ADR-O-003**: Hexagonal architecture (ports & adapters)
- **ADR-O-004**: SOLID principles (all components)
- **ADR-O-005**: VCG allocation (game-theoretic optimal)

**See**: `docs/adr/INDEX.md`

---

## Project Structure

```
okr-executive-system/
├── README.md (this file)
├── pyproject.toml (Python package config)
├── requirements.txt (dependencies)
├── requirements-dev.txt (dev dependencies)
├── Makefile (developer commands)
├── .github/workflows/ (CI/CD)
│
├── src/okr_executive/ (Main package)
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── domain/ (Domain models)
│   │   ├── models.py (OKRModel, GoalModel, etc.)
│   │   ├── events.py (All event types)
│   │   └── exceptions.py (Domain exceptions)
│   ├── engines/ (Core 6 engines)
│   │   ├── base.py (ExecutionEngine interface)
│   │   ├── okr_engine.py (Phase 1: Parse OKRs)
│   │   ├── research_engine.py (Phase 2: Research)
│   │   ├── planning_engine.py (Phase 3: Plan)
│   │   ├── execution_engine.py (Phase 4: Execute)
│   │   ├── review_engine.py (Phase 5: PR)
│   │   └── metrics_engine.py (Phase 6: KPIs)
│   ├── adapters/ (Infrastructure)
│   │   ├── event_broker.py (NATS JetStream)
│   │   ├── repository.py (DuckDB)
│   │   ├── github_adapter.py (PR submission)
│   │   └── kanban_adapter.py (Task tracking)
│   └── orchestrator/ (Coordination)
│       ├── okr_orchestrator.py (Main orchestrator)
│       └── state_machine.py (OKR lifecycle)
│
├── tests/
│   ├── unit/ (Unit tests - 1 test file per module)
│   │   ├── test_models.py
│   │   ├── test_okr_engine.py
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── integration/ (End-to-end tests)
│   │   └── test_e2e_pipeline.py
│   └── fixtures.py (Shared test fixtures)
│
├── docs/
│   ├── ARCHITECTURE.md (System design)
│   ├── DEVELOPMENT.md (How to build each phase)
│   ├── API.md (API reference - when ready)
│   └── adr/ (Architecture Decision Records)
│       ├── INDEX.md (ADR registry)
│       ├── ADR-001-*.md
│       └── ...
│
└── scripts/
    ├── setup_dev.sh (Development setup)
    ├── run_tests.sh (Test runner)
    └── lint.sh (Code quality)
```

